    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` so the registration date now also rolls forward past public holidays.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. Added a fixed public-holiday set (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:123`):\n   ```java\n   private static final java.util.Set<LocalDate> PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS = java.util.Set.of(\n       LocalDate.of(2026, 1, 1), LocalDate.of(2026, 1, 26), LocalDate.of(2026, 4, 25),\n       LocalDate.of(2026, 12, 25), LocalDate.of(2026, 12, 28));\n   ```\n\n2. Updated `toBusinessDay(...)` to keep rolling forward while the adjusted date is a weekend **or** a listed holiday, plus a small `isWeekend` helper. This correctly chains cases (e.g. a holiday falling on a Friday continues past the following weekend to Monday):\n   ```java\n   LocalDate adjusted = switch (date.getDayOfWeek()) { ... };\n   while (isWeekend(adjusted) || PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS.contains(adjusted)) {\n       adjusted = adjusted.plusDays(1);\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. Updated the Javadoc to describe the holiday roll-forward.\n\nThe daily-limit grouping and bulk-signup warning both route through `toBusinessDay`, so they automatically respect holidays as well. `./mvnw -o test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with all tests passing, including the acceptance test asserting the default registration date is never a weekend.",
